<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Seeb</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Agreement of Seeb</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Seeb was an agreement concluded in 1920, through British mediation, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscat">Muscat</a> and the tribal leaders of the Ibadi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imamate">Imamate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> in the interior. It ended the fighting that had begun with the imamate's rising in 1913 and left the interior largely self-governing. Its meaning was disputed in the 1950s, when the sultan reasserted control of the interior.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-seeb.jpg" alt="Treaty of Seeb" width="320" height="323" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: British National Archive · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1920_Treaty_of_Seeb.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
